[{"description":"Armenian Arts and Film London launches a new series of cross-disciplinary events at Bush Theatre — starting with poetry and sound.\r\nOne of Perla Kantarjian's poems is archived on the Moon, sent up as part of the Lunar Codex. Lebanese-Armenian, writing in her third language, English, she's been racking up prizes — from the Bridport Prize to the National Poetry Competition — and was the sole Sonny Mehta Scholar chosen from the MENA region at UEA. The Guardian calls her work \"fierce and bristling with life.\" Her debut, You Must Become Field (Bad Betty Press), lands in the UK this September, moving from 1915 Constantinople to a 2025 Beirut club bathroom — and from language to language, the way memory does.\r\n\"I come from a family that was already once made homeless by history,\" Kantarjian says. \"Writing is how I hold the small and the vast in one hand.\"\r\nJoining her: Olivia Melkonian, sound artist and founder of Analog Armenia, an open-access archive preserving Armenian cassette culture — endangered dialects, folk songs, revolutionary broadcasts, sourced from Lebanon, Armenia and community contributions. Melkonian traces her own fragmented Lebanese-Armenian heritage through the recordings she saves.\r\nTwo archivists, different mediums — one in language, one in tape. Expect poetry and music alongside the conversation, followed by drinks in the Bush Theatre's welcoming cafe. \r\nArmenian Arts and Film London supports and promotes Armenian and diasporan artists, filmmakers, and creatives through cultural and educational programmes. MIXTAPE is a series of events assembled by Armenian Arts and Film London to give a platform to new voices in the arts and beyond. Co-sponsored by Bad Betty Press and the International Armenian Literary Alliance (IALA).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/1b6f076e-add3-4bb3-95ff-6477901cd366.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"ALT B: MIXTAPE: Live with Perla Kantarjian & Olivia Melkonian","instanceDates":"3 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/1b6f076e-add3-4bb3-95ff-6477901cd366-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"124454ADDLLLJBNKHVKQDKBHRBPMJJQDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"We recommend arriving around 20 minutes before the show is due to begin. Check your journey before you travel.","attribute_Genre":"Poetry/Live Music","attribute_Interval":"No","attribute_Isovertureperformance":false,"attribute_Season":"ALT B","attribute_SeasonGrouping":"ALT B","attribute_Ticketsforgoodevent":false,"attribute_TicketVenue":"Attic","attribute_WebsiteCategorisation":"Alt B","attribute_FinancialCapacity":null},{"description":"Following a series of sold-out performances, Talking People returns to the Bush for five nights of fearless, unscripted theatre.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"ALT B: Talking People","instanceDates":"14 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"124254ABVRJVJPNQKPPNJBJRGDBMVHBTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-14T19:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-14T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T19:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"We recommend arriving around 20 minutes before the show is due to begin. Check your journey before you travel.","attribute_Genre":"Drama","attribute_Interval":"Yes","attribute_Isovertureperformance":false,"attribute_Season":"ALT B","attribute_SeasonGrouping":"ALT B","attribute_Ticketsforgoodevent":false,"attribute_TicketVenue":"Studio","attribute_WebsiteCategorisation":"Alt B","attribute_FinancialCapacity":null},{"description":"A queer play about why and how we choose to pay attention. Co-created by acclaimed director Jules Head and Bruntwood Prize shortlisted writer Georgia Bruce.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/508ff45b-1eeb-4a4c-af40-46ac2c27b027.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"ATTENTION","instanceDates":"19 November-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/508ff45b-1eeb-4a4c-af40-46ac2c27b027-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"122254AJRMSMDLKNQSHDJBHQRCTDCGDLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-23T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"We recommend arriving around 20 minutes before the show is due to begin. Check your journey before you travel.","attribute_Genre":"New Writing","attribute_Interval":"No","attribute_Isovertureperformance":false,"attribute_Season":"Bush Season 26/27","attribute_SeasonGrouping":"2026 Season","attribute_Ticketsforgoodevent":false,"attribute_TicketVenue":"Studio","attribute_WebsiteCategorisation":"Production","attribute_FinancialCapacity":null},{"description":"This performance is Audio Described. Would you like to pre-book your Audio Description headset for this show?","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\tThis performance is Audio Described. Would you like to pre-book an <span class=\"BoldText\">Audio Description headset</span>?\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/5b16b34e-1be7-460f-b861-bd03f896095f.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Audio Description Headset","instanceDates":"18 February-13 March","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/bushtheatre/files/5b16b34e-1be7-460f-b861-bd03f896095f-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"73654ANVTMBKPHMTBCRMSTGDTJPJHGDGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-18T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeU